{"content":[{"c":["JEHOVAH-TSIDKENU*"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Name of the righteous king of David’s line who God promised would rule over his people (",{"href":"?bref=Jer.23.5-6","r":"Jer.23.5-6","rawR":"Jer.23.5-6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.23.5-6","value":"Jer.23.5-6"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jer 23:5-6"},"). The name means “The ",{"c":["Lord"],"sourceClass":"divine-name","t":"span"}," (Yahweh or Jehovah) is our righteousness.” It was also applied to the king’s subjects, who will profit by his reign (",{"href":"?bref=Jer.33.16","r":"Jer.33.16","rawR":"Jer.33.16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.33.16","value":"Jer.33.16"}],"t":"ref","v":"33:16"},"). To Christians, God’s promise finds its fulfillment in Christ, who is Lord of all and the believer’s righteousness."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"JehovahTsidkenu","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Jer 23:5-6","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Jer.23.5-6","rawQueryValue":"Jer.23.5-6","sourceRefExact":"Jer.23.5-6"},{"anchorText":"33:16","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Jer.33.16","rawQueryValue":"Jer.33.16","sourceRefExact":"Jer.33.16"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"1112146a2332b664108076d8773612f14fca48881cb5d62d60cc0c7d47cb709d","sourceItemName":"JehovahTsidkenu","sourceItemOrder":160,"sourceMember":"Articles/J.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"JehovahTsidkenu","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Jehovah-Tsidkenu*","title":"Jehovah-Tsidkenu*","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}